  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 138 PM MST TUE NOV 3 2026\nTroughing moving onto the coast of British Columbia on Friday, \npaired with a building ridge over California, will shunt the \nmajority of tropical moisture coming in on an atmospheric river \nto the north. This flow will keep our area dry throughout much\nof the period. Periodic short-waves will work to break down the\nridge beginning early next week, but with much of the moisture\nwrung out in the Cascades, the only tangible evidence would be\nincreased mid-high cloud cover. Uncertainty in pattern evolution\nincreases come Tuesday, although cluster analysis favors the\npattern persisting.",
